  "title": "Post Hurricane Harvey vessel removal",
  "description": "The Coast Guard helped to remove over 165 vessels after Hurricane Harvey struck havoc in the waterways of the affected areas. The Coast Guard also helped to remove over 58,000 gallons of oil from the same waterways. Petty Officer 1st Class Nick Debrum, a marine science technician from Coast Guard Marine Unit Houma, discusses what he and other Coast Guard members did to protect the public and the environment.",
